 ### Smoothstep SDF Blend
-A technique to blend between two SDFs based on the distance of the query point from the origin, using a smooth interpolation factor [S2, unofficial]. It uses `smoothstep` to create a spatially varying blend factor $s$ that transitions from 0 to 1 as the distance from the origin increases from 0.0 to 1.0 [S2, unofficial]. This creates a radial blend zone. The function returns a `vec2` containing the blended distance and a primitive identifier (typically 1) [S2, unofficial].
